WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.620
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.420
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.580
We're The Office Ladies.

8
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.570
Hi there.

9
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:31.950
Guys, thank you so much for your support of our podcast and watching with us and listening with us.

10
00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.810
It means so much, and we are loving all of your comments, too.

11
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:35.810
It has been so fun.

12
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:40.150
And I have loved going through the comments and going through the questions and the mailbox.

13
00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:44.990
By the way, if you want to send us a question, you can send it to officeladies at earwolf.com.

14
00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:45.830
All right.

15
00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:49.550
Today, we are moving into Season 2.

16
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:50.010
Woo!

17
00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:57.810
Season 2, Episode 1, The Dundies, written by Mindy Kaling, directed by Greg Daniels.

18
00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:58.210
Yes.

19
00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:03.670
And you guys out there listening, we really wanted to do a live podcast of this at Achilles.

20
00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:05.170
Yes, we did.

21
00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:10.410
As it turns out, a lot of stuff is involved in doing that, and we just didn't get it together in time.

22
00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:13.010
But we do plan on doing some live podcasts.

23
00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.970
Yes, and maybe we'll go to Achilles.

24
00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:16.230
We have to make that happen.

25
00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:17.150
We have to make it happen.

26
00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:17.670
For sure.

27
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.070
You're allowed back in now.

28
00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:19.750
I am.

29
00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.210
They lifted the ban officially.

30
00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:21.970
They did.

31
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:25.250
Like a year and a half ago, so I can now go to Achilles.

32
00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:26.930
So we have to make that happen.

33
00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:27.090
Yeah.

34
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.410
There is so much to talk about with this episode.

35
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:35.150
I have so many notes, and I'm looking at my notes, and I realize the one thing I don't have is a summary written down.

36
00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:36.710
What is wrong with you?

37
00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:41.050
I was so excited to get into the episode that I failed to write a summary, so here we go.

38
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:41.810
I'm going to wing it.

39
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:50.690
In this episode, manager Michael Scott gives out awards to his employees called the Dundies during a very awkward show at Achilles.

40
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:52.210
How did I do?

41
00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.370
You did pretty great.

42
00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.310
He thinks he's like, you know, an amazing stand-up comedian, performer.

43
00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:01.590
I did see that a Dundie, I saw a description online of what a Dundie is.

44
00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:01.910
Okay.

45
00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:03.790
So if you look up Dundie, it says,

46
00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:08.830
A Dundie is an award bestowed annually by Dunder Mifflin Scranton, regional manager Michael Scott.

47
00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:12.570
In order to maintain morale, everybody gets a Dundie.

48
00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:13.830
Where did you read that?

49
00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:14.790
I did it.

50
00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.730
There's a thing called Dunderpedia.

51
00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:17.350
Oh!

52
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.550
Well, let's start with this fast fact.

53
00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:19.810
Okay.

54
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.210
It's also a fan question.

55
00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.870
Erin asked, where did the idea for the Dundies come from?

56
00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.090
I don't know.

57
00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:33.930
The Dundies were based on an awards presentation that Greg Daniels did for his real-life employees on King of the Hill.

58
00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.170
Oh, my gosh.

59
00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.710
He was the Michael Scott of King of the Hill.

60
00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.230
Greg!

61
00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:43.350
He gave them out in a ceremony, and they were called the Swampies.

62
00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:44.330
Oh, my Lord.

63
00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:49.730
And he gave out the same businessman statues that Michael gives out.

64
00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:56.710
He went into a trophy shop, and he saw those statues, and it inspired him to do an award show for his employees.

65
00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:01.110
And then, now, it graduated into an idea for the office.

66
00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:03.730
I actually can really see Greg doing that.

67
00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:08.950
I can see him going and buying them and thinking, like, it would, like, boost everyone's spirits.

68
00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.550
Yes, it was a morale booster.

69
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.010
Aw, Greg.

70
00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.870
This leads me into fast fact number two.

71
00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:20.570
The Dundies was the story that Greg wanted to use as the season one, episode one pilot.

72
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:21.770
Instead of?

73
00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.170
Instead of the pilot.

74
00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:23.630
Yes.

75
00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:31.550
This was his idea for how to kick off the American version of the office, but the network said they preferred we do an adaptation of the British pilot.

76
00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:32.350
Wow.

77
00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.510
And Greg was very, very disappointed.

78
00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:42.030
But if you notice, and Angela, maybe you did notice, there has been a Dundie on Michael's desk from the very beginning.

79
00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:47.230
It's in our opening credits, and Michael Scott, all through season one, had a Dundie.

80
00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.990
It's in the opening credits, but is it on his desk in the episode?

81
00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:51.810
Oh, well, now that I don't know.

82
00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:56.070
See, because I don't think it's on his actual desk, but I think it's in the credits.

83
00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.030
It's in the credits.

84
00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:57.370
Yes.

85
00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:02.850
But I do think that even that little bit is that way where Greg had something in his head.

86
00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:03.190
Right.

87
00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:11.190
He had this idea of these Dundie Awards looming for all this time, and finally, when we got picked up, he was able to do something with it.

88
00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:12.950
Oh, my goodness, we got a second season.

89
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.510
That would really have been a bummer.

90
00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.670
Or else that little shot in the opening credits would have remained a mystery.

91
00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.110
What is the little man on his desk?

92
00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:20.390
What's the little man with the briefcase?

93
00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.190
What is it?

94
00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.990
Are we ready for fast fact number three?

95
00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.090
We're moving more quickly than I thought we would.

96
00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.250
Well, let me just tell you, I'm just letting you go, lady.

97
00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:27.730
All right.

98
00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.370
Jenna, I wish you guys could see her.

99
00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.530
She came in what looks like a mechanic's outfit.

100
00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:33.390
Yeah, it's my green jumpsuit.

101
00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:33.930
Her green jumpsuit.

102
00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:35.090
But I also have a hat on.

103
00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:35.590
A hat on.

104
00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.430
Because I think I look like I could assemble something.

105
00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:44.050
Maybe.

106
00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:45.070
Okay, go, go, go.

107
00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.710
All right, fast fact number three.

108
00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:51.070
The second season of The Office was originally only six episodes long.

109
00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:52.630
We only got picked up for six episodes.

110
00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:53.230
I know.

111
00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.770
We were so excited to get six.

112
00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.930
But after that, we're like, well, I guess that's it.

113
00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.050
That might be all.

114
00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:01.150
But they started airing, and then they ordered three more.

115
00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.910
Then they ordered four more.

116
00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:03.390
Right.

117
00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:08.550
Then I think they ordered the rest of the whole season, and we ended up with a usual amount of time.

118
00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.670
Yeah, but in the beginning, we were like, well, we got six.

119
00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.290
Well, that's that.

120
00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.570
Oh, no, we got three more.

121
00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:17.290
Oh, we got, you know, it kind of gave you that sense of like, well, we might as well go for it,

122
00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.730
because we don't know if we're going to have this job.

123
00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:20.130
Yeah.

124
00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:25.310
And this episode of The Dundies was actually the third episode that we shot when we came back,

125
00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:29.970
and it was the first episode that we ever shot away from our office set.

126
00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:30.290
Yes.

127
00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:33.930
This was the first time we went on a completely different location.

128
00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:35.610
It was really, really cool.

129
00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:41.570
And we shot this the week after Steve Carell's movie, The 40-Year-Old Virgin, hit theaters.

130
00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:42.370
Yes.

131
00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:45.110
It was the number one movie at the box office.

132
00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.350
We were so excited for him.

133
00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:51.030
And Steve, being the sweetheart that he is, invited the whole entire cast to the premiere.

134
00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:51.510
Yeah.

135
00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.290
And we all went, and we got dressed up.

136
00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:58.010
And that was like one of the first fancy movie anything parties I've ever been to.

137
00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.070
I have a crazy story about that, Angela.

138
00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:00.270
What?

139
00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:04.350
Well, we had been shooting all day, and then the premiere was that night.

140
00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:04.690
Yeah.

141
00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:09.170
And we got dressed on set, and the hair and makeup people did our hair and makeup.

142
00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:09.430
Yeah.

143
00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.670
And we carpooled, and we went to this premiere.

144
00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:16.870
And when we got there, I was wearing this dress.

145
00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.470
It's very hard to explain.

146
00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:20.950
Maybe we can find a photo of it and put it on our website.

147
00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:25.670
It was sort of like a lacy mermaid thing.

148
00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:29.010
It was like green and blue.

149
00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:29.690
What?

150
00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:33.090
I don't even remember where I got it or how I got it.

151
00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.750
It was my first big movie premiere.

152
00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:36.150
Right.

153
00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:39.550
I didn't know what you were supposed to wear or how you were supposed to dress.

154
00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:45.850
It was a silky dress, and then over it had a lace part.

155
00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:48.970
So the silk part was like the slip, and then the lace part went over.

156
00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:49.160
Yes.

157
00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:50.010
A silk slip.

158
00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:50.950
Thank you, Angela.

159
00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.890
And it was blue and green, sort of mermaid-y colors, I guess.

160
00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:55.430
Oh, well.

161
00:06:55.530 --> 00:07:00.890
And it had this really big ribbon around the hips.

162
00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.950
What is happening with this dress?

163
00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:03.530
But I'll tell you.

164
00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:07.230
And then it had the ribbon tassels were hanging down in the front.

165
00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:07.490
In the front.

166
00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:07.870
Okay?

167
00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:08.230
Okay.

168
00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:11.050
So when we got to the premiere, I had to pee so badly.

169
00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:16.830
So before we walked the red carpet, I ran into the bathroom, and I peed very quickly.

170
00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.110
Did you pee on the ribbon?

171
00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.450
I did not pee on the ribbon.

172
00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:19.690
Okay.

173
00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.210
No, that would have been awful.

174
00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.650
That's where I thought the story was going.

175
00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.370
No, the ribbon did not dip in the toilet.

176
00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:24.790
Okay.

177
00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:26.870
But, you know, that happens sometimes.

178
00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.850
Yeah, I said that because I feel like it's happened to me.

179
00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:29.210
Okay.

180
00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:31.990
I did not pee on the ribbon, but I was rushing.

181
00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:35.450
And I came back out, and I went to the red carpet.

182
00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:36.650
I took my pictures.

183
00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:37.590
I posed.

184
00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:37.950
Yeah.

185
00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:38.670
I did the pictures.

186
00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:39.530
Whirlwind.

187
00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:40.830
Hoped I did it right.

188
00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:42.010
Went inside.

189
00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:48.370
When I got inside, I realized that I had tucked the slip into my underwear.

190
00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:48.930
No.

191
00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.170
And I had—

192
00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:52.630
Was your butt showing in the lace in the photos?

193
00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:54.690
No, my butt was not showing.

194
00:07:55.110 --> 00:08:00.830
Thankfully, that ribbon was strategically poised to cover my lady bits.

195
00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:01.730
Oh, Jenna.

196
00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:10.260
Because it was just lace on the bottom because I had tucked the slip into my underwear, but

197
00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.160
it gets worse.

198
00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:11.780
What?

199
00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.980
How can it get worse than you tucked your—

200
00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:18.080
Also, didn't you feel some air in places you should have been feeling air?

201
00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.440
I was so nervous.

202
00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:20.100
You were rushing.

203
00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.120
You were rushing.

204
00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:21.860
Okay, okay, okay.

205
00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:24.840
I wanted to get into my friend Steve's big movie premiere.

206
00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.080
Okay, how does it get worse?

207
00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:31.260
You know when you go and you buy, like, the three-pack of cotton underwear at Target?

208
00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:32.020
All the time.

209
00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:37.000
And there's a white pair, a black pair, a new pair, and then a crazy-colored pair?

210
00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.440
I was wearing the crazy pair.

211
00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:40.500
Oh, Jenna.

212
00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.300
From my Target underwear pack.

213
00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.080
And I think, like, from the back, you must have been able to see it.

214
00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:52.720
Thankfully, I didn't turn around on the red carpet, but I'm sure many people saw that

215
00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:53.680
as I was walking.

216
00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.500
Jenna, I do not remember if I did the red carpet or not.

217
00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:57.640
I don't know if I did.

218
00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.760
I think I just went in the theater.

219
00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:03.260
I mean, I would have to go back and look, but I feel like I didn't even know that we

220
00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:04.080
had to do that.

221
00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:05.880
Someone made me do it.

222
00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:09.780
Like, I got out of the car and, you know, someone grabbed me and said,

223
00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:10.800
you need to take pictures.

224
00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:15.900
I'm pretty sure I drove myself, and I just parked in the garage, and I walked in.

225
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:21.660
But I just remember being so excited for Steve, and he was so happy we were there.

226
00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:25.600
He had us all sitting together, and he came over, and he gave us all a big hug.

227
00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:27.780
And I kind of remember that he wore a white suit.

228
00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:28.980
Am I remembering that right?

229
00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:29.440
Don't know.

230
00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:29.980
Don't know.

231
00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:30.860
Should have looked it up.

232
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.580
We were doing the Dundies today.

233
00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.680
I don't think I bought anything new.

234
00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.060
I don't remember what I wore.

235
00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:41.500
I sat between John and Rain at the premiere when the movie was over.

236
00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:47.740
I turned to John, and I said, Steve is going to be the biggest movie star when this movie

237
00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:48.220
comes out.

238
00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:48.500
Yeah.

239
00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:49.680
He's going to stop being Steve.

240
00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:51.540
He's going to start being Steve Carell.

241
00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:52.580
Yeah.

242
00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.620
And it's going to be weird, because we know Steve.

243
00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:56.160
Right.

244
00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:00.300
And the rest of the world is going to know Steve Carell in about one week.

245
00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:03.520
I remember thinking, like, holy moly, this is going to be a big hit.

246
00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.340
So now we're shooting the Dundies.

247
00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:05.860
Yes.

248
00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:11.140
The 40-year-old virgin has come out, and as predicted, Steve is Steve Carell.

249
00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:12.360
He's a huge movie star.

250
00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:18.820
And since we're on location, they had to economize space, and we were each given these teeny,

251
00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.020
teeny, tiny trailers.

